WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.601
-With just four weeks to go

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.901
until the pivotal
midterm elections

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:07.501
and early voting about to start
in some crucial states,

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.567
Republicans and Democrats
have settled

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.100
on very different strategies.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.968
Republicans in key
battleground races

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.367
that will determine control
of Congress

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.467
have decided to fully embrace
Donald Trump,

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.300
even as the federal
criminal investigation

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.100
into his stolen classified
documents intensifies.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.200
President Biden, meanwhile,
is taking the first steps

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.734
towards decriminalizing
marijuana.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.834
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:31.801
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:36.100
As much as we may all want him
to disappear into the sunset,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.734
Donald Trump is still
very much playing

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.634
a central role
in Republican politics

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.067
and, specifically,
the GOP's campaign

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.467
to take back control
of Congress.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:46.467
Just this weekend, he traveled
to Nevada and Arizona,

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.834
two crucial battleground states

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.067
with tight races
for both governor and Senate,

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.634
and yet, even though Trump
is theoretically supposed

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.601
to be there to campaign
for other candidates,

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:57.968
he always, without exception,
makes it about himself.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter ]
He's like the best man
at a wedding

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.601
who gives a drunken toast
about how awesome he is.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:04.734
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ As Trump ] I remember

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.801
when Jake came up to me
sophomore year.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.200
Big guy, strong guy, tears,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.834
[ Laughter ]
tears pouring down his face,

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.567
and he said to me,
he told me he just met Sarah

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.033
and he needed advice from me

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:18.133
because I was the smartest
and sexiest guy he knew.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.634
And I told him -- I told him
these exact words.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:22.567
He'll remember it.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:23.968
[ Laughter ]
I told him.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.767
He'll remember.
I said, "If you love her,

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:29.133
you got to get a ring and lock.
-[Both] her. up!

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.167
[ Laughter and applause ]
For example,

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.167
Trump was in Nevada on Saturday
to campaign

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.133
with the GOP candidates
for Senate and governor,

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.534
Adam Laxalt and Joe Lombardo,
who both got up to speak.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:41.801
After Lombardo's remarks,
he could be heard asking Trump

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.834
if he should stay
up onstage with him

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.334
and I want you to guess
Trump's response.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:47.767
-Thank you, sir.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:50.367
[ Whistling ]

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.033
-Thank you, sir.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:53.934
-Okay, sir.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:55.167
[ Laughter ]
-Thanks, sir.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.033
-[ As Trump ]
No, no, no, no.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.000
Off, off you go...

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.167
You thought Donald Trump would
share a stage with you?

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:06.300
This is a guy who once literally
shoved another world leader...

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.701
...at a NATO summit to get
to the front of the group.

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.701
I'm shocked Trump didn't pick
Lombardo up over his head

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:15.501
and throw him off the stage
WWE-style.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.634
Also, I love how sheepishly
he asked Trump

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.968
if he should stay
up there with him.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.334
He's like an actor
asking a table of producers

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.667
if he can audition
a second time.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:24.901
"Do you, um --
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:26.334
Do you want me
to do that line again?"

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.000
Uh, no. You can, uh, just get
the [bleep] on outta here.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.634
And you can actually, uh,
take the head shot.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:35.968
[ Laughter ]
And then

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.033
on Sunday,
Trump went to Arizona,

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.234
ostensibly, to campaign

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:40.667
with Blake Masters
and Kari Lake,

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.467
the GOP candidates
for Senate and governor.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.267
But again, he could not help
but rant about his own problems,

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.267
including the federal
criminal investigation

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.534
into the classified documents
he stole from the White House.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:52.067
Now, any normal person
in that situation

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.167
might stay out of the spotlight
or, at the very least,

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:55.701
avoid talking about the case
in public.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.667
But Trump, as we all know,
is not normal

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:58.834
and, during that rally
in Arizona,

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.234
Trump decided just essentially
to confess.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:05.100
-I had a small number of boxes
in storage at Mar-A-Lago,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.968
guarded by Secret Service
and my people and everybody.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.234
I mean, it's safe.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:11.234
There is no crime.
You know, there is no crime.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.834
It's not a crime.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.634
And they should give me,
immediately, back

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.033
everything that they've taken
from me

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.701
[ Laughter ]
because it's mine. It's mine.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:19.701
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.834
They took it
from me in the raid.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.767
They broke into my house!

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.934
-The key quote there is
when he says, "It's mine."

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.868
That shows you it wasn't just
some misunderstanding.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.634
He didn't take the classified
documents by accident.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.868
He took them on purpose because
he thinks they belong to him.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:34.667
And, when you're proving
a crime, criminal intent is key.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.834
I know that because I watch
a show called...

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.434
[ Laughter ]
It's right there in the title.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:40.934
There was never a "Law &amp; Order"
spinoff called...

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:48.601
And then Trump decided
to reel off a truly insane story

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.667
about what other presidents
had done

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:52.934
with their own
presidential records.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:55.200
-George H.W. Bush

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.834
took millions
of documents

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.300
to a former bowling alley

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.767
and a former Chinese restaurant,

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:01.133
where they combined them,

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:04.868
so they're in a bowling alley/
Chinese restaurant.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:11.734
-Now, usually, this would be
the part of "A Closer Look"

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.901
where I carefully dissect
that insanity,

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:16.834
but instead, I want to see
what it would feel like

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.801
to actually believe him.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.634
[ Laughter ]
Which brings us
to a new segment called

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.267
"Seth Takes Donald Trump
at His Word."

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.434
[ Shimmering tune plays ]
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.067
You know what?

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:28.133
When you tell me
George H.W. Bush

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.367
took millions of documents

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.901
to a bowling alley/
Chinese restaurant,

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.267
I believe you.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.634
I believe you
because I don't think

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.868
you'd ever make
something up like that.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.834
[ Laughter ]
And here's how I believe
it happened.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.734
George H.W. Bush
was leaving office

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:43.067
and packed up millions
of documents,

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.567
loaded them into what was
probably multiple trucks.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:46.701
And then his family
came out and said,

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:48.200
"Whoa, Dad!

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.601
What are you doing?!"

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.634
And he said,
"I'm in a super bad mood

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.267
about only serving one term.
Get out of my way!"

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.167
And they said, "You can't just
take all these documents."

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.033
And he said,
"Not only am I taking them,

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:01.868
I am taking them to a bowling
alley/Chinese restaurant...

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.734
...where I intend to spend
my retirement picking up spares,

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.300
knocking down wontons,

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.167
and reading state secrets
at my leisure!

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:12.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:13.968
And if you think I'm turning
these trucks around,

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.000
let me assure you I'm --"

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.100
[ As Dana Carvey's Bush ]
Not gonna do it.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
At which point,

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:21.200
Barbara turned to her kids
and she said, "You know what?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.300
Just let him go."

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.968
[ Laughter ]
And that is why,

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:27.033
to this day, if you're in Texas,
you can stop by...

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:32.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:36.634
This has been "Seth Takes
Donald Trump at His Word."

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:38.133
[ Shimmering tune plays ]

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.734
Got to say, you guys,
it's pretty fun.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.868
I can see why people
at his rallies

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:45.000
are having such a good time.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:47.834
Again, I want to emphasize

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:50.634
these aren't obscure appearances
we have to go digging for.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:51.934
These are rallies
Trump is holding

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.767
with GOP candidates
in key battleground states

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.000
to win back control of Congress.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.968
He thinks he's actually
helping those candidates.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:05:59.000
Biden, meanwhile, is taking

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.200
an entirely
different approach --

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.501
doing things people like.

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.400
For example,
polls have repeatedly shown

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.901
that voters overwhelmingly say
marijuana should be legal

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:07.601
for medical
and recreational use.

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:10.100
And last week, Biden took
an important first step

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.901
toward decriminalizing
marijuana.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:14.033
-President Biden is taking
his first major steps

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.467
toward
decriminalizing marijuana.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:17.667
Today, he pardoned thousands
of Americans convicted

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:19.167
on federal possession charges,

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:21.834
simple possession cases,
dating back to the 1990s.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:24.968
-That clears
about 6,500 people convicted

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:28.133
between 1992 and 2021.

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:31.200
And he is also urging governors
to pardon those convicted

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.634
of state charges, which make up

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:34.901
for the vast majority
of convictions.

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.167
The president is also
ordering his administration

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:39.934
to review how marijuana
is classified,

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:42.767
saying that it makes no sense
that it is a Schedule I drug

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:46.167
in the same class
as heroin and LSD.

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:49.434
-You know, Biden always had
that vibe of a grandpa who,

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.567
if he caught you smoking weed,
would scold you

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:53.200
and then take a long hit...

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.701
...before telling you
he spent a summer

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:58.667
as a roadie
for Grand Funk Railroad.

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
This is obviously huge news

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.367
and a long overdue first step
toward criminal justice reform

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:07.033
and undoing the racist
and disproportionate impacts

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:08.801
of our deeply inhumane
drug laws.

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:10.767
No one should be in jail
for something you can buy

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:12.200
at a boutique in Beverly Hills.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.400
There are states in this country

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.701
where you can find
a high-end weed dispensary

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.501
with all kinds of fancy edibles

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:18.801
in a strip mall right next
to a...

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:21.367
-Bowling alley/
Chinese restaurant.

00:07:21.367 --> 00:07:23.634
[ Laughter and applause ]
-But on top of being
the right thing to do,

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:26.901
it might also explain a lot
because there have been times

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:28.501
when Biden has gotten stuck
onstage

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:30.334
in a way that makes me think

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:33.367
he might've just taken
a giant bong rip...

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.767
...and the weed is just starting
to kick in.

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.267
[ As Biden ]
Whoa!

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:41.100
Can anyone like see me?
Am I --

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.000
Did I turn into a statue?

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:47.868
And then there's this moment
from Thursday, where,

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:49.367
for some reason,
Biden just started

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:51.434
silently backing away
from reporters,

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:53.868
once he decided he didn't want
to answer any more questions.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:04.434
-No, the trip was not
essentially for oil.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:05.834
The trip was
about the Middle East

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:07.367
and about Israel and --

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:09.701
and rationalization
of positions.

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:11.267
But it is a disappointment

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:13.567
and it says
that there are problems.

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:15.133
-Are you worried about --
-[ Clamoring ]

00:08:15.133 --> 00:08:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:21.734
-What is he doing?

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:24.534
Is he trying to do
the Homer Simpson meme?

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:27.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:27.067 --> 00:08:29.167
You can't --
You can't disappear.

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:31.701
You're on camera

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:33.868
in front of the most famous
building in the world.

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:35.934
We can all see you.

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:38.400
It's like trying
to Irish goodbye a meeting

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.434
in your own office.

00:08:39.434 --> 00:08:40.534
[ Laughter ]
So,

00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:42.133
those are the quarterly
sales reports.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:43.467
A little bit lower
than we expected.

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:45.534
And now, before I answer
what I assume will be

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.801
some very angry
shareholder questions,

00:08:47.801 --> 00:08:49.000
I'm just going to head
to the bathroom

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.801
and I will be right back.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:53.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:59.601
And I'll just wait here

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:01.167
until they're gone.

00:09:01.167 --> 00:09:02.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.267 --> 00:09:03.667
And then after, I guess,

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:05.567
attempting to moonwalk
away from reporters,

00:09:05.567 --> 00:09:07.968
[ Laughter ]
Biden made this
unfortunate gaffe

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:09.734
at a manufacturing event
on Friday.

00:09:09.734 --> 00:09:12.300
-Let me start off
with two words --

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.234
Made in America.

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:15.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:17.701
Made in America.

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:19.467
-[ As Biden ]
Greatest band ever?

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:20.367
[ Inhaling sharply ]

00:09:20.367 --> 00:09:21.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:23.267
Two words --

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:25.434
Grand Funk Railroad.

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:27.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:27.234 --> 00:09:30.167
Now, even though this news
was both hugely popular

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:33.100
and a big step toward a fairer
and more sane drug policy,

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:35.133
it won't surprise you to learn
that not everyone was pleased.

00:09:35.133 --> 00:09:37.200
Specifically,
Fox News had some issues,

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.167
although I'm not sure
they all made sense.

00:09:39.167 --> 00:09:42.267
-Joe is rolling out
a political Hail Mary

00:09:42.267 --> 00:09:45.734
and today, one year after firing
or suspending dozens

00:09:45.734 --> 00:09:48.801
of White House staffers
for past marijuana use,

00:09:48.801 --> 00:09:51.701
well, Biden announced
a widespread pardon

00:09:51.701 --> 00:09:55.367
to anybody convicted
of marijuana possession

00:09:55.367 --> 00:09:56.501
on the federal level.

00:09:56.501 --> 00:09:57.868
-Well, it starts
with marijuana,

00:09:57.868 --> 00:09:59.200
but where does it go from there?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.167
-I think it's so cynical
because the question

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:03.367
of the impact
of drugs on our kids

00:10:03.367 --> 00:10:05.701
and our societies is immense.

00:10:05.701 --> 00:10:07.634
-Now, I want to describe
the left's midterm agenda

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:09.634
very simply.
You ready?

00:10:09.634 --> 00:10:11.067
This is what they're going
to give you more of,

00:10:11.067 --> 00:10:13.100
if you elect them --

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.868
abortion, pot, porn,

00:10:15.868 --> 00:10:18.033
and more January 6th hearings.

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:19.801
-Man, sounds awesome.

00:10:19.801 --> 00:10:22.367
Just add in a bowling alley/
Chinese restaurant.

00:10:22.367 --> 00:10:23.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:23.667 --> 00:10:25.133
Feel like that's
a great night out.

00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:28.067
It's so funny, how right-wing
pundits always have this way

00:10:28.067 --> 00:10:30.501
of making Democrats sound better
than they actually are.

00:10:30.501 --> 00:10:32.901
Also, where did the porn thing
come from?

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:34.167
[ Laughter ]
Did they just

00:10:34.167 --> 00:10:36.067
throw that in there
without any good reason?

00:10:36.067 --> 00:10:38.901
Is there some secret
pro-porn legislation proposed

00:10:38.901 --> 00:10:41.067
by Chuck Schumer
that I'm not aware of?

00:10:41.067 --> 00:10:43.000
[ Laughter ]
Because he definitely
lowers his glasses

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.334
like a guy who's seeing porn
for the very first time.

00:10:46.334 --> 00:10:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.267 --> 00:10:48.367
[ As Schumer ]
Yowza, that is

00:10:48.367 --> 00:10:50.434
some pretty steamy stuff.

00:10:50.434 --> 00:10:51.968
[ Laughter ]
Also,

00:10:51.968 --> 00:10:53.267
check out this graphic

00:10:53.267 --> 00:10:55.234
Sean Hannity put
up on the screen.

00:10:55.234 --> 00:10:58.100
Why does Fox keep accidentally
making Joe Biden look cooler

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.434
than he actually is
with their graphics?

00:10:59.434 --> 00:11:00.868
[ Laughter ]
I mean, last week,
Tucker Carlson

00:11:00.868 --> 00:11:02.801
aired this badass graphic

00:11:02.801 --> 00:11:04.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
of Biden eating ice cream

00:11:04.667 --> 00:11:07.133
in front of a burning building
and now, Hannity airs this.

00:11:07.133 --> 00:11:09.033
This looks like something
you'd have up on the wall

00:11:09.033 --> 00:11:10.434
in your college dorm room.

00:11:10.434 --> 00:11:11.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:11.934 --> 00:11:14.367
So, with the midterms looming,
Republicans and Democrats

00:11:14.367 --> 00:11:16.234
have clearly settled
on different strategies.

00:11:16.234 --> 00:11:17.634
Biden's trying to appeal
to voters

00:11:17.634 --> 00:11:20.300
with policies that are
overwhelmingly popular in polls,

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.234
like reforming marijuana laws;

00:11:22.234 --> 00:11:24.033
while Republicans embrace
Donald Trump,

00:11:24.033 --> 00:11:25.801
even as he rants
about bowling alleys

00:11:25.801 --> 00:11:28.100
and Chinese restaurants,
like a guy who's on...

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.968
-Heroin and LSD.

00:11:29.968 --> 00:11:31.334
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.334 --> 00:11:33.067
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:33.067 --> 00:11:36.667
♪♪

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:38.467
The midterm elections
are coming up, so,

00:11:38.467 --> 00:11:41.067
to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:44.133
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:11:44.133 --> 00:11:48.133
to check your voter registration
status or to register to vote.

